            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.19.21</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Sign in with an account.</b> Signing in opens your browser, where you
      can use an email code or Google — and create an account if you don't have
      one yet. You land back in Jarvis by yourself; the app comes to the front
      when the browser is done.</li>
  <li><b>You can back out of a sign-in.</b> If the browser goes nowhere — a
      wrong link, a closed tab — a Stop button ends the attempt instead of
      leaving the button spinning for three minutes.</li>
  <li><b>The sign-in screen has a sky.</b> Stars drift behind Jarvis, and he
      looks around while he waits for you. The tab your browser lands on after
      signing in matches it.</li>
  <li><b>Fixed:</b> returning from the browser could leave you with two Jarvis
      windows open at once.</li>
  <li><b>Fixed:</b> signing out could quietly fail and leave you signed in.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
